$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To the ketophosphonate 41 (331 mg, 0.49 mmol) in THF (1.2 mL) was added
barium hydroxide (93 mg, 0.54 mmol) and stirred for 30 minutes at room
temperature Aldehyde 7 (126 mg, 0.44 mmol) was added in 40:1 THF:H2O (2 ×
1 mL) and the yellow mixture was stirred for 12 hours at room
temperature. The reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl (5
mL). The quenched reaction mixture was transferred to a separatory funnel
and extracted with Et2O (3 × 10 mL). The combined organic extracts were
washed with brine (5 mL), dried with Na2SO4 and concentrated by rotary
evaporation to give a colorless oil that was purified by flash column
chromatography (Hexanes:EtOAc = 8:1) to give 42b. Colorless oil; Yield:
240 mg (67%, 77% based upon recovered starting material). 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.25 (d, J= 9.0 Hz, 2H), 6.87 (d,
J= 9.0 Hz, 2H), 6.62 (t, J= 6.8 Hz, 1H), 4.64 (d, J= 11.3 Hz, 1H), 4.61
(d, J= 11.3 Hz, 1H), 4.48 (s, 2H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 3.69 (m, 2H), 3.65 (ddd,
J= 8.5, 5.7, 3.1 Hz, 1H), 3.54 (dd, J= 5.0, 3.1 Hz, 1H), 3.45 (m, 2H),
3.41 (m, 1H), 3.39 (s, 3H), 2.66 (m, 2H), 2.29 (dt, J= 15.0, 6.0 Hz, 1H),
2.16 (s, 3H), 2.04 (m, 1H), 1.95 (dd, J= 12.3, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 1.78 (m, 2H),
1.76 (s, 3H), 1.62 (m, 3H), 1.48 (m, 2H), 1.41 (m, 1H), 0.93 (d, J= 6.7
Hz, 3H), 0.91 (d, J= 6.9 Hz, 3H), 0.89 (s, 9H), 0.88 (s, 9H), 0.87 (d, J=
7.1 Hz, 3H), 0.06 (s, 3H), 0.05 (s, 3H), 0.04 (s, J= 3.0 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, Acetone-d6) δ 201.48, 160.09, 141.38, 138.40, 131.61, 129.82,
114.36, 78.95, 77.33, 76.79, 73.73, 73.29, 72.86, 60.17, 57.47, 55.41,
39.94, 39.04, 38.14, 36.51, 35.65, 33.85, 30.64, 27.54, 26.54, 26.27,
20.86, 19.00, 18.69, 16.54, 14.32, 11.71, 11.64, 1.32, -3.39, -3.59,
-5.23; HRMS (ESI) calculated for C43H80O7SSi2 (M+Na) 819.5061, found
819.5064.
