$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 47: To a stirred solution of phosphonate 5 (67 mg, 0.21
mmol) in THF (1 mL) at -45 °C was added LiHMDS (1M in THF, 0.189 mL, 0.19
mmol). The yellow clear solution was stirred at -45 °C for 30 minutes and
at -78 °C for 20 minutes. Aldehyde 46 (31 mg, 0.045 mmol) in THF (1 mL)
was added at -78 °C, and then the resulting solution was stirred at -78
°C for 30 minutes, -40 °C for 30 minutes and-4°C for 10 minutes. The
reaction mixture was quenched with NH4Cl (2 mL), and extracted with Et2O
(3 × 3 mL). The combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried
with Na2SO4 and concentrated by rotary evaporation to give a light yellow
oil that was purified by flash column chromatography (Hexanes:EtOAc =
15:1) to give the above dienoate. Colorless oil; Yield: 27 mg (77%, 4E:4Z
= 14:1). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.25 (dd, J= 15.5, 10.0 Hz, 1H), 7.25
(d, J= 8.0 Hz, 2H), 6.87 (d, J= 8.7 Hz, 2H), 6.24 (dd, J= 15.3, 10.7 Hz,
1H), 6.18 (dt, , J= 15.3, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.80 (d, J= 15.4 Hz, 1H), 5.32 (t,
J= 7.1 Hz, 1H), 4.61 (d, J= 11.5 Hz, 1H), 4.59 (d, J= 11.5 Hz, 1H), 4.48
(s, 2H), 4.19 (q, J= 7.2 Hz, 2H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 3.60 (t, J= 3.5 Hz, 1H),
3.56 (td, J= 6.7, 3.4 Hz, 1H), 3.47-3.42 (m, 3H), 3.40 (s, 3H), 3.36 (t,
J= 7.0 Hz, 1H), 3.13 (s, 3H), 2.44 (dt, J= 15.5, 4.5 Hz, 1H), 2.29 (dt,
J= 15.5, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 2.14 (s, 3H), 1.83 (m, 2H), 1.64 (m, 1H), 1.56-1.37
(m, 5H), 1.49 (s, 3H), 1.29 (t, J= 7.1 Hz, 3H) , 0.90 (d, J= 6.9 Hz, 3H),
0.88 (s, 9H), 0.87 (d, J= 6.9 Hz, 1H), 0.83 (d, J= 7.0 Hz, 2H), 0.05 (s,
3H), 0.04 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.20, 159.13, 144.61,
140.55, 135.13, 130.40, 129.18, 127.63, 119.73, 113.72, 88.12, 78.95,
78.54, 75.72, 73.22, 73.00, 72.07, 60.21, 57.38, 55.64, 55.24, 39.60,
38.77, 37.44, 34.67, 33.48, 31.75, 30.26, 28.66, 26.07, 20.24, 18.41,
15.54, 14.35, 14.29, 10.95, 10.40, -3.69, -3.88; HRMS (ESI) calculated
for C44H76O8SSi (M+Na) 815.4917, found 815.4928.
