$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: diethyl (2E,4E)-octa-2,4-dien-1-ylphosphonate
(5b). Sulfonylphosphonate 2e (259 mg, 0.65 mmol, 1 equiv.) was dissolved
in THF (2.6 mL, 0.25 M) and cooled to -78 °C. KHMDS (155 mg, 0.78 mmol,
1.2 equiv., 1 M in THF) was added slowly. After five minutes at -78 °C,
propionaldehyde (70 μL, 0.97 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added to the solution.
After 20 minutes, the reaction mixture was warmed up to 0 °C. After 1
hour, the reaction was quenched by addition of aqueous NH4Cl solution and
the product was extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with
brine, dried over MgSO4, and then concentrated in vacuo. The reaction
mixture was purified by column chromatography (grad. 15%→30% acetone in
hexanes). (114 mg, 0.49 mmol, 76%, 91:9 EE:EZ by 1H NMR) as a colorless
oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.14 (ddd, J = 5.0, 10.4, 15.2 Hz, 1H),
6.02 (dd, J = 10.6, 15.1 Hz, 1H), 5.68 (dtd, J = 2.3, 6.5, 15.2 Hz, 1H),
5.51 (dt, J = 7.3, 14.9 Hz, 1H), 4.10 (m, 4H), 2.62 (dd, J = 7.6, 22.3
Hz, 2H), 2.09 (qn, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 1.31 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 6H), 1.00 (t, J
= 7.5 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 136.2 (d, J = 4.3 Hz), 135.3
(d, J = 14.9 Hz), 128.5 (d, J = 4.7 Hz), 119.3 (d, J = 12.5 Hz), 61.9 (d,
J = 6.7 Hz), 30.6 (d, J = 140.0 Hz), 25.6, 16.4 (d, J = 5.8 Hz), 13.4;
HRMS (ES) m/z calcd for C11H21O3P [M+H]+ 233.1301, found 233.1301; IR
(thin film, cm-1) 3019, 2966, 2933, 2907, 2874, 1478, 1457, 1443, 1392,
1368, 1252, 1212, 1164, 1098, 1058, 1028, 989, 962, 844, 811, 790.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective (EE:EZ=91:22), alternative preparation
shown, Julia-Kocienski olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

