$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure B: Preparation of Trisubstituted Olefins To a
flame-dried round bottom flask equipped with a magnetic stir bar was
added freshly prepared lithium diisopropyl amide (LDA, 19.0 mg, 0.174
mmol) in dry THF. The solution was cooled to -78 °C. Under the Barbier
conditions,1 a solution in THF of 6h (26 mL, 0.237 mmol) and 5 (50.0 mg,
0.158 mmol) was added slowly to the LDA/THF solution at -78 °C. The
reaction was stirred overnight, approximately 15-18 hours while warming
to room temperature, until the reaction deemed complete by TLC analysis.
The reaction was quenched on saturated ammonium chloride solution in
water, extracted with ethyl acetate (3x), washed with brine, dried over
magnesium sulfate, and concentrated in vacuo. The resulting crude
material was purified using silica gel chromatography (ethyl
acetate/pentane) to afford 4h. Compound 4h was prepared by General
Procedure B to afford a homogeneous clear oil in 75% yield and >95:5 Z
stereochemistry as evidenced by 1-D Nuclear Overhauser effect
spectroscopy (NOE) and 1H NMR spectroscopy. 1H-NMR(CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ
7.13-7.00 (m, 7H), 6.99-6.98 (m, 2H), 6.46 (s, 1H), 2.35 (s, 3H), 2.20
(s, 3H); 1H NMR NOE (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 6.46 1H <-> 2.20 3H (4.9%); 2.20
3H <-> 6.46 1H (6.8%); 13C-NMR(CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 139.2, 138.9, 138.0,
136.8, 129.4, 129.2, 128.1, 128.0, 126.5, 126.2, 27.4, 21.5; IR (film
cm-1) 3019, 2964, 2919, 2859, 1509, 1439, 1374, 1109, 916, 861, 816, 750,
694; Exact mass calcd for [M+H] requires m/z 208.1252 Found 208.1248
(ES+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Julia olefination, Barbier conditions, Z:E g.t. 95:5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Markovnikov-Selective Hydrothiolation of Styrenes: Application to the
Synthesis of Stereodefined Trisubstituted Olefins
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Savolainen, Markku A.; Wu, Jimmy
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(14), 3802-3804

