$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-diethyl (4-methylpent-2-en-1-yl)phosphonate (6d). Sulfonylphosphonate
3 (246 mg, 0.66 mmol, 1 equiv.) was dissolved in THF (2.6 mL, 0.25 M) and
cooled to -78 °C. KHMDS (157 mg, 0.79 mmol, 1.2 equiv., 1 M in THF) was
added slowly. After five minutes at -78 °C, isobutyraldehyde (90 μL, 0.99
mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added to the solution. After 20 minutes, the
reaction mixture was warmed up to 0 °C. After 1 hour, the reaction was
quenched by addition of aqueous NH4Cl solution and the product was
extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried over
MgSO4, and then concentrated in vacuo. The reaction mixturewas purified
by column chromatography (grad. 15%→30% acetone in hexanes). (106 mg,
0.48 mmol, 72%, >95:5 E:Z by 1H NMR) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (500MHz,
CDCl3) δ 5.57 (ddd, J = 6.3, 6.3, 15.3 Hz, 1H), 5.36 (dt, J = 7.2, 14.9
Hz, 1H), 4.09 (m, 4H), 2.54 (dd, J = 7.3, 21.4 Hz, 2H), 2.30 (m, 1H),
1.31 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 6H), 0.98 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 143.1 (d, J = 14.5 Hz), 115.6 (d, J = 11.3 Hz), 61.8 (d, J = 6.9
Hz), 31.2 (d, J = 2.0 Hz), 20.4 (d, J = 139.4 Hz), 22.3 (d, J = 3.4),
16.4 (d, 5.9 Hz); HRMS (ES) m/z calcd for C10H21O3P [M+H]+ 221.1301,
found 221.1302; IR (thin film, cm-1) 2960, 2932, 2907, 2870, 1467, 1445,
1392, 1366, 1253, 1164, 1098, 1060, 1029, 965, 867, 789, 712.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective (E:Z=>95:5), Julia-Kocienski olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

