$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical procedure for difluoromethylenation of carbonyl compounds with
reagent 3 (Table 1, entries 8, 13): Under N2 atmosphere, 0.9 mL LHMDS (1M
in THF, 1.8 equiv) was added to a solution of 4-phenylbutan-2-one (7m)
(111 mg, 0.75 mmol, 1.5 equiv ) and 2-(Difluoromethylsulfonyl)pyridine 3
(96 mg, 0.5 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in DMF (2 mL) at -50 oC. The reaction
mixture was allowed to warm up to rt . Then, the reaction is quenched
with aqueous saturated ammonium chloride (1 mL), followed by 3N HCl
(1mL). The completion of the reaction was monitored by 19F NMR (for entry
8, the reaction mixture was heated to 60 oC for 30 min). After extraction
with Et2O, the organic phase was successively washed with brine, and then
dried over anhydrous MgSO4. After the solution was filtered and the
solvent was evaporated under vacuum, the residue was subjected to silica
gel column chromatography to give product 8m (65 mg, 0.36 mmol, yield:
72%) as a colorless oil. 8m, yield 72% 1H NMR: δ 7.15-7.35 (m, 5H), 2.70
(t, J = 8.1 Hz ,2H), 2.27 (td, J = 7.5 Hz, J = 1.5 Hz, 2H), 1.58 (t, J =
3.3 Hz, 3H). 19F NMR: δ -96.74 (d, J = 58.1 Hz, 1F), -97.09 (d, J = 56.7
Hz, 1F). MS (EI, m/z): 182 (M+, 1.2), 155 (75.0), 152 (36.5), 140 (58.0),
137 (76.4), 109 (100.0), 65 (54.1), 44 (46.9).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Difluoromethyl 2-Pyridyl Sulfone: A New gem-Difluoroolefination Reagent
for Aldehydes and Ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhao, Yanchuan; Huang, Weizhou; Zhu, Lingui; Hu, Jinbo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(7), 1444-1447

