$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (9E,11E)-methyl 13-(diethoxyphosphoryl)trideca-9,11-dienoate (9).
Sulfonylphosphonate 2e (904 mg, 2.26 mmol, 1 equiv.) was dissolved in THF
(9.04 mL, 0.25 M) and cooled to -78 °C. KHMDS (505 mg, 2.71 mmol, 1.2
equiv., 1 M in THF) was added slowly. After five minutes at -78 °C,
(E)-methyl 10-iododec-9-enoate 2 (496 mg, 2.49 mmol, 1.2 equiv., 1 M in
THF) was added to the solution. After 20 minutes, the reaction mixture
was warmed up to 0 °C. After 1 hour, the reaction was quenched by
addition of aqueous NH4Cl solution and the product was extracted with
EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and
then concentrated in vacuo. The unpurified reaction mixture was purified
by column chromatography (grad. 15%→30% acetone/hexanes). (570 mg, 1.58
mmol, 70% yield; 91:9 EE:EZ by 1H NMR) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR
(500MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.13 (ddd, J = 4.9, 10.4, 15.1 Hz, 1H), 6.01 (dd, J =
10.8, 15.0 Hz, 1H), 5.62 (dt, J = 7.6, 14.7 Hz, 1H), 5.50 (dt, J = 7.5,
14.9 Hz, 1H), 4.14-4.05 (m, 4H), 3.66 (s, 3H), 2.61 (dd, J = 7.6, 22.3
Hz, 2H), 2.30 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 2.07-2.01 (m, 2H), 1.67-1.56 (m, 2H),
1.39-1.23 (m, 14H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 174.3, 135.3 (d, J = 14.9
Hz), 134.7 (d, J = 4.3 Hz), 129.5 (d, J = 4.6 Hz), 119.2 (d, J = 12.5
Hz), 61.9 (d, J = 6.7 Hz), 51.4, 34.1, 32.5 (d, J = 1.3 Hz),30.6 (d, J =
139.9 Hz), 29.1 (d, J = 1.5 Hz), 29.1, 29.1, 29.0, 24.9, 16.4 (d, J = 5.9
Hz); HRMS (ES) m/z calcd for C18H33O5P [M+H]+ 361.2138, found 361.2144;
IR (thin film, cm-1) 3019, 2982, 2929, 2855, 1739, 1438, 1392, 1367,
1251, 1210, 1167, 1098, 1056, 1028, 989, 961, 841, 807, 780, 710.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective (E:Z=91:9), Julia-Kocienski olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

