$DATUM diethyl ((2E,4E)-6,6-dimethylhepta-2,4-dien-1-yl)phosphonate (5g).
Sulfonylphosphonate 2e (228 mg, 0.57 mmol, 1 equiv.) was dissolved in THF
(2.3 mL, 0.25 M) and cooled to -78 °C. KHMDS (136 mg, 0.68 mmol, 1.2
equiv., 1 M in THF) was added slowly. After five minutes at -78 °C,
pivaldehyde (93 μL, 0.85 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added to the solution.
After 20 minutes, the reaction mixture was warmed up to 0 °C. After 1
hour, the reaction was quenched by addition of aqueous NH4Cl solution and
the product was extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with
brine, dried over MgSO4, and then concentrated in vacuo. The reaction
mixture was purified by column chromatography (grad. 15%→30% acetone in
hexanes). (104 mg, 0.40 mmol, 70%, >95:5 EE:EZ by 1H NMR) as a colorless
oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.13 (ddd, J = 4.9, 10.2, 15.1 Hz, 1H),
5.95 (dd, J = 10.3, 15.5 Hz, 1H), 5.66 (dd, J = 2.3, 15.5 Hz, 1H), 5.52
(dt, J = 7.5, 14.9 Hz, 1H), 4.10 (m, 4H), 2.61 (ddd, J = 1.1, 7.6, 22.2
Hz, 2H), 1.32 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 6H), 1.02 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 145.6 (d, J = 4.4 Hz), 135.7 (d, J = 14.7 Hz), 124.4 (d, J = 4.9 Hz),
119.3 (d, J = 12.7 Hz), 61.9 (d, J = 6.4 Hz), 33.1 (d, J = 1.5 Hz), 30.6
(d, J = 139.9 Hz), 29.5 (d, J = 1.0 Hz), 16.4 (d, J = 5.9 Hz); HRMS (ES)
m/z calcd for C13H25O3P [M+H]+ 261.1614, found 261.1616; IR (thin film,
cm-1) 3026, 2957, 2904, 2867, 1476, 1462, 1444, 1392, 1364, 1333, 1253,
1216, 1164, 1098, 1055, 1029, 990, 961, 874, 846, 831, 812, 784, 712.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective (EE:EZ=>95:5), Julia-Kocienski
olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

