$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM diethyl ((2E,4E)-5-cyclopentylpenta-2,4-dien-1-yl)phosphonate (5f).
Sulfonylphosphonate 2e (248 mg, 0.62 mmol, 1 equiv.) was dissolved in THF
(2.5 mL, 0.25 M) and cooled to -78 °C. KHMDS (148 mg, 0.74 mmol, 1.2
equiv., 1 M in THF) was added slowly. After five minutes at -78 °C,
cyclopentanecarbaldehyde (0.10 mL, 0.93 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added to
the solution. After 20 minutes, the reaction mixture was warmed up to 0
°C. After 1 hour, the reaction was quenched by addition of aqueous NH4Cl
solution and the product was extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was
washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and then concentrated in vacuo. The
reaction mixture was purified by column chromatography (grad. 15%→30%
acetone in hexanes). (137 mg, 0.50 mmol, 81%, 95:5 EE:EZ by 1H NMR) as a
colorless oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.13 (ddd, J = 4.9, 10.5, 15.1
Hz, 1H), 6.01 (dd, J = 10.5, 15.1 Hz, 1H), 5.63 (ddd, J = 2.2, 7.8, 15.1
Hz, 1H), 5.50 (dt, J = 7.5, 15.0 Hz, 1H), 4.10 (m, 4H), 2.61 (dd, J =
7.6, 22.3 Hz, 2H), 2.44 (sext, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 1.82-1.74 (m, 2H),
1.69-1.52 (m, 4H), 1.34-1.24 (m, 8H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 139.4
(d, J = 3.9 Hz), 135.4 (d, J = 15.2 Hz), 127.6 (d, J = 4.9 Hz), 119.2 (d,
J = 12.7 Hz), 61.9 (d, J = 6.9 Hz), 43.3, 33.1 (d, J = 1.5 Hz), 30.6 (d,
J = 139.9 Hz), 25.1, 16.5 (d, J = 6.0 Hz); HRMS (ES) m/z calcd for
C14H25O3P[M+H]+ 273.1614, found 273.1615; IR (thin film, cm-1) 3021,
2978, 2953, 2908, 2868, 1478, 1445, 1392, 1367, 1253, 1213, 1164, 1098,
1058, 1028, 987, 961, 842, 808, 782, 711, 665.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective (EE:EZ=95:5), Julia-Kocienski olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME310 STEP1
$RXN



