$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 42a and 42b: Methyl lithium (46 μL, 0.14 mmol, 3M in
(EtO)2CH2 was added to a clear colorless solution of (CF3)2CHOH (15 μL,
0.144 mmol) in (MeOCH2)2(0.6 mL) at 0 °C under Ar and stirred for 10
minutes. The above solution was transferred via cannula to neat 41 (84
mg, 0.13 mmol) and the mixture was stirred for 30 minutes at room
temperature under Ar, followed by addition of aldehyde 34 (26 μL, 0.16
mmol). The reaction was stirred for 48 hours then quenched with 5 % HCl
(10 mL). The quenched reaction mixture was transferred to a separatory
funnel and extracted with CHCl3 (2× 20 mL). The combined organic extracts
were dried with Na2SO4 and concentrated by rotary evaporation to give a
yellow oil that was purified by flash column chromatography
(Hexanes:EtOAc = 8:1) to give 42a. Colorless oil; Yield: 58 mg (66%). 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 6.62 (t, J= 7 Hz, 1H), 4.64 (d, J= 11.5 Hz, 1H),
4.63 (d, J= 11.5 Hz, 1H), 3.84 (t, J= 4.2 Hz, 1H), 3.77 (s, 3H), 3.67 (m,
3H), 3.54 (dd, J= 3, 4.5 Hz, 1H), 3.39 (s, 3H), 2.69 (m, 2H), 2.32 (dt,
J= 5.5, 14.5 Hz, 1H), 2.17 (s, 3H), 2.10 (m, 1H), 1.96 (m, 1H), 1.89 (m,
1H), 1.78 (s, 3H), 1.78 (obscured multiplet, 1H), 1.70 (t, J= 7 Hz,
2H),1.62 (m, 3H), 1.42 (m, 1H), 0.96 (d, J= 7 Hz, 3H), 0.92 (d, J= 6.5
Hz, 3H), 0.90 (s, 9H), 0.89 (s, 9H), 0.87 (d, J= 6.5 Hz, 3H), 0.07 (s,
3H), 0.052 (s, 3H), 0.046 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (C6D6, 75 MHz) δ 200.3, 172.7,
139.5, 138.8, 79.2, 77.1, 76.3, 73.5, 59.9, 57.7, 51.2, 40.2, 38.5, 38.0,
35.6, 35.1, 33.6, 30.2, 30.0, 26.9, 26.4, 26.2, 20.3, 18.7, 18.4, 16.5,
14.3, 11.9, 11.7, -3.4, -3.5, -5.2; HRMS (ESI) calculated for
C36H72NaO7SSi2 (M+Na) 727.4435, found 727.4443.
