$DATUM tert-Butyl
(R,R,R,E,E)-2-hydroxy-3-[N-benzyl-N-(α-methylbenzyl)amino]-8-phenylocta-4,7-dienoate
25. KHMDS (0.5 M in PhMe, 0.47 mL, 0.24 mmol) was added dropwise to a
solution of 27(66 mg, 0.11 mmol, greater than 99:1 dr) and PhCHO (13 μL,
0.13 mmol) in THF (2.5 mL) at -78 °C, and the resultant mixture was
stirred at -78 °C for 30 min. H2O (2 mL) was then added, and the reaction
mixture was allowed to warm to rt. The aqueous layer was then extracted
with Et3O (3 x 10 mL), and the combined organic extracts were
washedsequentially with satd aq NH4Cl (20 mL) and brine (20 mL) and then
dried and concentrated in vacuo to give 25 in greater than 99:1 dr.
Purification via flash column chromatography (eluent 30-40 °C
petrol/Et3O, 10:1). Product 25 as a pale yellow oil, yield 35 mg, 66%,
greater than 99:1 dr. [α]25D -49.6 (c 1.0 in CHCl3); νmax (ATR) 3499
(O-H), 3083, 3066, 3026, 2977, 2933, 2824 (C-H), 1722 (C=O), 1600 (C=C);
δH (500 MHz, CDCl3) 1.33 (9H, s, CMe3), 1.40 (3H, d, J 6.8, C(α)Me), 2.96
(2H, app t, J 6.6, C(6)H2), 3.61 (1H, dd, J 9.1, 2.5, C(3)H), 3.83 (1H,
d, J 14.5, NCHAHBPh), 3.99 (1H, d, J 14.5, NCHAHBPh), 4.14 (1H, d, J 2.5,
C(2)H), 4.26 (1H, q, J 6.8, C(α)H), 5.58 (1H, dt, J 15.5, 6.6, C(5)H),
5.79 (1H, dd, J 15.5, 9.1, C(4)H), 6.17 (1H, dt, J 15.9, 6.6, C(7)H),
6.41 (1H, d, J 15.9, C(8)H), 7.18-7.45 (15H, m, Ph); δC (125 MHz, CDCl3)
15.1 (C(α)Me), 27.9 (CMe3), 36.0 (C(6)), 51.4 (NCH2Ph), 56.9 (C(α)), 62.9
(C(3)), 74.5 (C(2)), 82.0 (CMe3), 126.6, 126.7, 127.0 (p-Ph), 127.0
(C(4)), 126.0, 127.9, 128.0, 128.2, 128.4, 128.5 (o,m-Ph), 128.1 (C(7)),
130.9 (C(8)), 132.4 (C(5)), 137.5, 141.5, 144.1 (i-Ph), 172.7 (C(1)); m/z
(ESI+) 498 ([M + H]+, 100%); HRMS (ESI+) C33H40NO3+ ([M + H]+) requires
498.3003; found 498.3011.
