$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Olefin S8. To a solution of sulfone 3 (44 mg, 108 μmol) in THF (1.0 mL)
was added KHMDS (0.5 M in toluene, 82 μL, 41 μmol) and the mixture was
maintained for 10 minutes. To the solution was added a solution of
aldehyde 4b (27 mg, 27 µmol) in THF (270 + 200 µL rinse) via cannula and
the reaction was maintained for 20 minutes. After warming to rt over 2 h,
the reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl and extracted with
Et2O. The combined organic layer was washed with water and saturated
aqueous NaCl, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by silica gel column chromatography (hexanes/CH2Cl2= 10/1 to
7/1) afforded silyl ether S8. (20 mg, 65%), colorless syrup. Rf = 0.65
(hexane/CH2Cl2 = 5/1); IR (film) ν 2953, 2928, 2893, 2856, 1253, 1116,
1085, 835, 776 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3)δ 6.28(ddd, J= 16.8, 10.2,
10.2 Hz, 1H), 6.09-6.00(m, 4H), 5.71-5.60(m, 3H), 5.53(ddd, J= 15.6, 6.6,
6.6 Hz, 1H), 5.42 (dd, J= 15.6, 7.8Hz, 1H), 5.08(d, J= 16.8Hz, 1H),
