$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step-I (olefination): To a solution of
building block 4 (0.1g, 0.2 mmol) in dry DMF at 0°C, under nitrogen
atmosphere was added sodium hydride (0.012g, 0.3 mmol). The solution
turned reddish orange indicating the formation of carbanion. After 10 min
of stirring, a solution of aldehydes 13a-m (0.24 mmol, 1.2 eq) in DMF (1
mL) was added. The temperature of the reaction was gradually raised from
0°C to room temperature and stirring continued at room temperature for
4-5 h. The progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC and after
complete consumption of starting material; the reaction was quenched with
ice cold water (15 mL) and extracted with ethyl acetate (2×15 mL). The
combined organic extracts were washed with water (20 mL), brine (20 mL)
and dried over anhydrous sodium sulphate, filtered, and the filtrate was
concentrated under vacuum. The crude compound was subjected to column
chromatography using silica gel as stationary phase, and combination of
hexane/ethyl acetate as mobile phase gave the protected olefinated
products 14a-m. (E)-Methyl
2-acetoxy-4-methoxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-en-1-yl)-6-styrylbenzoate (14a)
(E)-Methyl
2-acetoxy-4-methoxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-en-1-yl)-6-(2-(pyridin-3-yl) vinyl)
benzoate (14k) Yield = 0.050g, (65.0%). R f = 0.1 (EtOAc-Hexanes 4:6);
yellow solid mp = 129-130°C IR (KBr Pellet); 2922, 1763, 1709, 1605,
1560, 1444, 1295, 1257, 1207, 1161, 1047 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ:
8.70 (s, 1H, ArH); 8.50 (s, 1H, ArH); 7.81 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H, ArH); 7.42
(d, J = 16.4 Hz, 1H, CH); 7.30 (bs, 1H, ArH); 7.01 (s, 1H, ArH); 6.94 (d,
J = 16.0 Hz, 1H, CH); 5.08 (bs, 1H, CH); 3.94 (s, 3H, OCH3); 3.88 (s, 3H,
OCH3); 3.24 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 2H, CH2); 2.30 (s, 3H, COCH3); 1.73 (s, 3H,
CH3); 1.67 (s, 3H, CH3) ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 169.1 (C); 166.7
(C); 159.8 (C); 149.0 (CH); 148.8 (CH); 148.4 (C); 136.5 (C); 133.0 (CH);
132.4 (C); 128.9 (CH); 127.6 (CH); 124.0 (C); 123.7 (C); 121.1(CH); 118.1
(C); 105.9 (CH); 56.0 (OCH3); 52.4 (OCH3); 25.8 (CH3); 23.6 (CH2); 20.8
(CH3); 17.9 (CH3) ppm. HRMS-ESI: Calcd. For C23H26 NO5 [M+H]+: 396.1811,
396.1800.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (E), Julia olefination
