$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Fluoroolefins 10; General Procedure.
Fluorinated BT-sulfone 7 (1.20 equiv) and aldehyde 9 (0.080-0.510 mmol,
1.00 equiv) were dissolved in anhyd THF (33 mL/mmol 9) at 0 °C. To the
mixture, LiHMDS (2.40 equiv) was added dropwise and stirred 1.5 h at 0
°C. The reaction was quenched with sat. aq NaHCO3 (10 mL/mmol 9) and
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 30 mL/mmol 9). The combined organic layers were
washed with brine (10 mL/mmol 9) and dried (Na3SO4). The solvent was
evaporated and the crude product was purified by column chromatography
(cHex-EtOAc).
1-[2-(4-Chlorophenyl)-2-fluorovinyl]-2-(trifluoromethyl)benzene as a
colorless oil, yield 0.062 g, 0.135 mmol, 65%. Rf = 0.77 (cHex). IR
(KBr): 3471, 2075, 2924, 1904, 1655, 1598, 1577, 1543, 1496,1456, 1404,
1354, 1316, 1209, 1162, 1122, 1095, 1064, 1036, 1011, 957, 887 cm-1. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 6.55 (dq, J = 1.7, 36.4 Hz, 1 H, CH=CF), 6.59
(dq, J = 1.8, 19.6 Hz, 1 H, CH=CF), 7.06 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 1 Harom), 7.12
(d, J = 3.8 Hz, 1 Harom), 7.09-7.16 (m, 1 Harom), 7.24-7.40 (m, 7 Harom),
7.33 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1 Harom), 7.46-7.52 (m, 1 Harom), 7.63 (d, J = 7.6
Hz, 1 Harom), 7.62-7.65 (m, 2 Harom), 7.90 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1 Harom). 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 101.5, 106.6, 124.3, 124.5, 125.9, 126.0,
126.1, 126.2, 127.0, 127.3, 127.4, 127.7, 128.1, 128.6, 129.0, 129.0,
129.4, 129.5, 129.7, 131.0, 131.1, 131.7, 131.8, 131.9, 135.6, 135.6,
157.2, 157.7.19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -113.8, -97.2, - 61.4, -59.8.
MS (70 eV, EI): m/z (%) = 302/301/300 (32/16/100, [M+]), 283/282/281
(1/4/2, [M - F+]), 265 (5, [M - Cl+]), 245 (15), 196 (28). HR-EIMS: m/z
calcd for C15H9ClF4: 300.0328; found: 300.0331.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 0.4:1.0 E:Z, fluoro-Julia-Kocienski olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel aromatic fluoro olefins via fluoro-Julia-Kocienski olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Allendoerfer, Nadine; Es-Sayed, Mazen; Nieger, Martin; Brase, Stefan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2010), (20), 3439-3448

