$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-(Trimethylsilylmethyl)allylsilanes 2a-e
(General Procedure): Benzoylated compounds 7a-e (0.16 mmol) were
dissolved in THF (1.5 ml) and DMPU (0.73 ml, 6 mmol) was added. After
degassing the solution carefully by three freeze-pump-thaw cycles, a
solution of SmI2 (9.6 ml, 0.96 mmol, 0.1 M in THF) was added at 0 °C.
After 2 h at room temperature, the reaction was diluted with ether and
decanted from the samarium salts, which were washed thoroughly with
ether. The combined organic layers were washed with a sat'd solution of
NH4Cl and the aqueous layers were extracted with ether (3x15 ml). The
combined organic extracts were dried, filtered and evaporated.
Purification by column chromatography on florisil with pentane afforded
compounds 2a-e. 1-(Trimethylsilyl)-2-(trimethylsilylmethyl)oct-2-ene as a
colorless liquid, yield 28 mg, 64%. Rf (EtOAc/hexane 1:15) = 0.95. IR: ν
= 2954, 2923, 2856, 1645, 1597, 1458, 1411, 1246, 1155, 1066, 961, 832,
767, 694 cm-1. MS (EI) m/z (%): 270 (30) [M+], 269 (100) [M+ -H], 187
(40) [CH(CH2TMS)2+], 181 (10), 139 (30) [M+ -H -TMS -C4H9], 125 (10) [M+
-CH3 -TMS -C4H9], 99 (30) [CH2=CHCH2SiMe2+], 73 (100) [SiMe3+]. C14H34Si2
(270.6) calcd: C 66.58, H 12.66; found: C 67.17, H 12.79. 1H NMR (400
MHz, C6D6) : δ = 4.84 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 1H, =CH), 1.93 (dt, J = 6.8, 6.3
Hz, 2H, =CHCH2), 1.53 (s, 2H, CH2SiMe3), 1.45 (s, 2H, CH2SiMe3), 1.31 (m,
6H, (CH2)3), 0.89 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H, CH3), 0.04 (s, 9H, SiMe3), 0.02 (s,
9H, SiMe3). 13C NMR (100 MHz, C6D6): δ = 135.8 (s, =C), 121.7 (d, CH=C),
33.3 (t, =CHCH2), 31.8 (t, CH2), 31.4 (t, CH2SiMe3), 30.3 (t, CH2), 25.1
(t, CH2CH3), 24.2 (t, CH2SiMe3), 15.3 (q, CH3), 0.1 (q, SiMe3).
