$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Olefination with N,N'-dimethylphosphonamide
(R)-21a, addition of AcOH at room temperature (Table 2, entry 2). To a
solution of phosphonamide (R)-21a (3.4 g, 10.6 mmol) in THF (30 mL) was
added n-BuLi (5.6 mL of a 1.6 M solution in hexanes, 8.96 mmol) at -78
°C. The mixture was stirred for two hours at -78 °C, then ketone 17 (800
mg, 4.76 mmol) was added to it. The reaction mixture was stirred for one
hour at -78 °C, after which it was allowed to warm to room temperature,
AcOH (3.0 mL) was added, and stirring continued for another 20 min. After
addition of saturated NaHCO3 solution and extraction with CH2Cl2, the
combined organic phase was dried and concentrated in vacuo. The residue
was purified by flash chromatography (hexanes: Et2O, 10:1 to 4:1). (E/Z =
6:1 by 1H NMR). As second fraction, 220 mg of ketone 17 (28%) was
recovered. Analytical pure samples of the TBS-olefins were obtained by
flash chromatography (hexanes: Et2O, 100:1 to 20:1); The E/Z ratio was
determined by 1H NMR analysis of the crude reaction mixture. 1.01 g (62%)
of an E/Z-mixture of TBS-olefins 24a as a colorless oil. Z -24 was
obtained as the first fraction and E-24 as the second one. tert-Butyl((S,
Z)-4-((2R,
6R)-6-ethyl-5-methyl-3,6-dihydro-2H-pyran-2-yl)-2-methylpent-3-enyloxy)dimethylsilane
Z-24a was obtained as a colorless oil. Olefination with
N,N'-dimethylphosphonamide (S)-21a (Table 2, entry 5). tert-Butyl((R,
E)-4-((2R,
6R)-6-ethyl-5-methyl-3,6-dihydro-2H-pyran-2-yl)-2-methyl-pent-3-
enyloxy)dimethylsilane (E -24b). Treatment of phosphonamide (S)-21a (128
mg, 0.4 mmol) with n-BuLi (0.24 mL of a 1.6 M solution in hexanes, 0.38
mmol) and ketone 17 (34 mg, 0.2 mmol) in THF (1.5 mL), followed by quench
with AcOH (0.2 mL, 3.49 mmol) at -78 ºC gave 43 mg of olefin 24b (63%,
E/Z > 19:1) as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.60–5.57 (m,
1H), 5.23 (d, J = 9.3 Hz, 1H), 4.10 (br s, 1H), 3.83 (dd, J = 10.7, 2.8
Hz, 1H), 3.52 (dd, J = 9.7, 5.7 Hz, 1H), 3.37 (dd, J = 9.7, 7.7 Hz, 1H),
2.65–2.54 (m, 1H), 2.17–2.07 (m, 1H), 1.97–1.88 (m, 1H), 1.83–1.74 (m,
1H), 1.70 (d, J = 1.3 Hz, 3H), 1.63–1.60 (m, 3H), 1.60–1.49 (m, 1H), 0.98
(d, J = 6.7 Hz, 3H), 0.94 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 0.91 (s, 9H), 0.06 (s,
3H), 0.05 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 136.3, 135.2, 127.5, 120.9,
78.1, 77.7, 67.8, 35.0, 30.2, 26.0, 25.7, 18.9, 18.4, 17.3, 12.9, 8.4,
-5.3, -5.4. IR (film, NaCl) 2958, 2929, 2896, 2857, 1471, 1463, 1255,
1119, 1090, 1051, 1031, 836, 775 cm-1. [α]20 D +39.8° (c 2.35, CHCl3). MS
(ESI) calcd for C20H39O2Si (M+H)+: 339.3, found 339.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, E:Z >19:1, Horner-Wadsworth-Emmons reaction
