$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-Olefin 24. To a solution of sulfone 5 (166.1 mg, 0.2998 mmol) in
THF/HMPA (4:1, v/v, 1.0 mL) cooled to −78 °C was added LHMDS (1.0 M
solution in THF, 0.290 mL, 0.290 mmol), and the resultant solution was
stirred at −78 °C for 20 min. To this solution was added a solution of
aldehyde 6 (93.8 mg, 0.133 mmol) in THF/HMPA (4:1, v/v, 0.350 mL), and
the resultant solution was allowed to warm to room temperature over a
period of 6.5 h. The reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl
solution at 0 °C, and the mixture was extracted with EtOAc. The combined
organic layer was washed brine, dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and
concentrated under reduced pressure. Purification of the residue by flash
chromatography (silica gel, 5 to 15% EtOAc/hexanes) gave (E)-olefin 24
(86.7 mg, 63%), aldehyde 5 (21.4 mg, 23%), and sulfone 6 (97.9 mg, 82%
recovery based on 24). Data for 24: [α]26 D +18.6 (c 2.10, CHCl3); IR
(film) 2937, 2863, 1610, 1513, 1463, 1371, 1248, 1089, 882, 822, 704
cm−1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.65—7.63 (m, 4H), 7.41—7.34 (m, 6H),
7.21 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 6.85 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 6.43 (dd, J = 14.2,
7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.19 (d, J = 14.2 Hz, 1H), 5.27—5.19 (m, 2H), 4.49 (d, J =
11.2 Hz, 1H), 4.24 (d, J = 11.2 Hz, 1H), 3.86—3.77 (m, 5H), 3.72 (m, 1H),
3.50—3.40 (m, 4H), 3.21 (m, 1H), 2.31—2.23 (m, 2H), 1.92—1.70 (m, 5H),
1.66 (m, 1H), 1.58—1.09 (m, 10H), 1.04—1.00 (m, 30H),0.99 (d, J = 6.5 Hz,
3H), 0.92 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.1, 146.1,
137.3, 135.5 (4C), 134.02, 133.97, 130.3, 129.6, 129.5 (2C), 129.2 (2C),
127.61 (2C), 127.60 (2C), 113.7 (2C), 85.2, 78.0, 75.9, 74.0, 72.3, 72.2,
70.4, 69.0, 60.5, 55.2, 44.0, 42.5, 42.1, 41.7, 41.5, 39.0, 33.3, 32.1,
31.5, 26.8 (3C), 23.6, 21.6, 19.2, 18.1 (6C), 16.8, 12.4 (3C); HRMS (ESI)
calcd for C56H85IO6Si2Na [(M + Na)+] 1059.4822, found 1059.4835.
