$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S,Z)-methyl 4-((tert-butyldimethylsilyl)oxy)pent-2-enoate (S3). A
solution of potassium t-butoxide (54 g, 481 mmol) in anhyd THF (800 mL)
was cooled in a dry ice-bath. After 10 min, methyl methyl
2-(bis(2,2,2-trifluoroethoxy)phosphoryl)acetate (161 g, 481 mmol) in THF
(200 mL) was added dropwise to the reaction mixture over 1 h. The
reaction mixture was allowed to stir at-78 °C (bath temp) for 1 h after
which the aldehyde S2 (686.7 g, 460 mmol) in THF (50 mL) was slowly added
and then allowed to stir for an additional 2 hrs. The reaction mixture
was quenched with cold water (500 mL) and diluted with tert-butyl methyl
ether (300 mL). The aqueous layer was separated and extracted again with
tert-butyl methyl ether (1x500 mL, 1x400 mL). The combined organic layers
were washed with water (400 mL), brine (400 mL) and dried over Na2SO4.
The solvent was concentrated and the residue was purified on a silica
column (2% tert-butyl methyl ether in hexane). 68 g (61%) of ester S3 as
an oil. All analytical data for this compound were identical with the
reported data in literature.4
