$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Fluoroolefins 10; General Procedure.
Fluorinated BT-sulfone 7 (1.20 equiv) and aldehyde 9 (0.080-0.510 mmol,
1.00 equiv) were dissolved in anhyd THF (33 mL/mmol 9) at 0 °C. To the
mixture, LiHMDS (2.40 equiv) was added dropwise and stirred 1.5 h at 0
°C. The reaction was quenched with sat. aq NaHCO3 (10 mL/mmol 9) and
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 30 mL/mmol 9). The combined organic layers were
washed with brine (10 mL/mmol 9) and dried (Na3SO4). The solvent was
evaporated and the crude product was purified by column chromatography
(cHex-EtOAc). 3-[2-(2-Bromophenyl)-1-fluorovinyl]-2-chloropyridine as a
colorless oil, yield 0.024 g, 0.078 mmol, 60%. Rf = 0.19 (Z), 0.25 (E)
(cHex-EtOAc, 99:1). IR (KBr): 3436, 3056, 2925, 2853, 1925, 1676, 1579,
1558, 1469, 1437, 1398, 1349, 1277, 1230, 1180, 1134, 1101, 1061, 1036,
1025, 1005, 947, 877 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 6.75-6.88 (m, 3
H, CH=CF, Harom), 6.99-7.07 (m, 3 Harom), 7.18 (m, 2 Harom), 7.37 (dd, J
= 7.2 Hz, 1 Harom), 7.48-7.58 (m, 3 Harom), 7.63 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1
Harom), 7.95 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1 Harom), 8.34-8.42 (m, 2 H, ArH-6). 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 111.7, 113.4, 122.2, 122.3, 124.1, 124.3, 127.4,
127.5, 129.0, 129.2, 129.4, 130.3, 130.3, 130.8, 132.4, 132.6, 132.8,
132.9, 133.1, 138.3, 139.3, 139.7, 140.8, 150.7, 153.8, 155.2. 19F NMR
(376 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -104.5, -92.8. MS (70 eV, EI): m/z (%) =
315/313/311 (17/66/54, [M+]), 278/276 (18/18), 232 (6, [M - Br+]), 197
(100). HR-EIMS: m/z calcd for C13H8BrClFN: 310.9512; found: 310.9511.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
