$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Trans-alkene 16. A round-bottomed flask was charged with PT sulfone 15
(4.2 g, 12.4 mmol), DME (100 mL) and cooled to -55 °C. Potassium
bis(trimethylsilyl)amide (0.5 M in toluene, 24.8 mL, 12.4 mmol) was added
drop wise over 10 min., and the reaction was stirred at -55 °C for a
further 1 h. Aldehyde 4 (2.9 g, 12.1 mmol) was then added neat at -55 °C
via syringe and the syringe was rinsed with THF (2 × 2 mL). The reaction
was stirred at this temperature for a further 1 h and then allowed to
warm to room temperature over 1.5 h. The reaction was quenched with water
(70 mL), the layers were separated, the aqueous layer was extracted with
Et2O (3 × 50 mL), and the combined organic layers were washed with brine
(50 mL) and dried (MgSO4). Column chromatography (1 : 4 EtOAc : Hexanes).
Yield: (2.6 g, 60%) as a clear, colourless liquid. Rf = 0.66 (6: 1
Hexanes: EtOAc). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 5.32 - 5.55 (m, 2H), 4.68 (q,
1H, J = 5.3 Hz), 4.47 (t, 1H, J = 5.9 Hz), 3.36 - 3.70 (m, 8H), 2.32
(ABMX, 2H), 1.98 (ABMXY, 2H), 1.52 - 1.58 (m, 2H), 1.29 - 1.39 (m, 10H),
1.30 (d, 3H, J = 5.4 Hz), 1.204 (t, 3H, J = 7.0 Hz), 1.201 (t, 6H, J =
7.1 Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ 133.5, 124.6, 102.8, 99.5, 65.3,
61.0 (2 signals), 60.6, 37.3, 32.7, 29.9, 29.5 (2 signals), 29.4, 29.1,
26.3, 19.9, 15.3 (3 signals). IR (KBr windows) cm-1: 2975 (s), 2929 (s),
1569 (w), 1444 (w), 1373 (m), 1342 (m), 1129 (s), 1061 (s). MS (EI) Major
peaks: 103 (base peak), 121, 163, 181, 207, 225, 253, 283, 299, 329, 343.
HRMS (m+ + H) calcd for C20H41O4 345.3006, found 345.3010.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Julia- Kocienski reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (3E)-Dodecen-12-olide, a Potential Pheromone Component of
the Emerald Ash Borer
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM MaGee, D. I.; Mayo, P. D.; Silk, P. J.; Beattie, B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2013), 43(10), 1368-1377

