$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Difluoromethylenation of pregnenolone 9 with reagent 3: Under N2
atmosphere, 0.45 mL LHMDS (1M in THF, 2.25 equiv) was added to a solution
of pregnenolone (9) (65 mg, 0.205 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and
2-(difluoromethylsulfonyl)pyridine 3 (77 mg, 2.0 equiv) in 2mL THF/HMPA
(10:1, v/v) at -78 oC. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm up to rt
in 18h. Then, the reaction was quenched with aqueous saturated ammonium
chloride (1 mL) and 3N HCl (1mL), followed by extraction with Et2O. The
organic phase was successively washed with brine, and then dried over
anhydrous MgSO4. After the solution was filtered and the solvent was
evaporated under vacuum, the residue was subjected to silica gel column
chromatography to give product 10 (41 mg, 0.117 mmol, yield: 57%) as a
white solid. 10, yield: (41 mg, 0.117 mmol, 57%) 1H NMR: δ 5.34-5.37 (m,
1H), 3.46-3.58 (m, 1H), 1.56 (t, J = 3.3 Hz), 1.01 (s, 3H), 0.64 (s, 3H).
19F NMR: δ -92.55 (d, J = 53.4 Hz,1F), -93.26 (d, J = 55.6 Hz, 1F ). MS
(EI, m/z): 350 (M+, 80.4), 332 (46.6), 317 (100.0), 231 (28.9), 213
(63.2).
