$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Fluoroolefins 10; General Procedure.
Fluorinated BT-sulfone 7 (1.20 equiv) and aldehyde 9 (0.080-0.510 mmol,
1.00 equiv) were dissolved in anhyd THF (33 mL/mmol 9) at 0 °C. To the
mixture, LiHMDS (2.40 equiv) was added dropwise and stirred 1.5 h at 0
°C. The reaction was quenched with sat. aq NaHCO3 (10 mL/mmol 9) and
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 30 mL/mmol 9). The combined organic layers were
washed with brine (10 mL/mmol 9) and dried (Na3SO4). The solvent was
evaporated and the crude product was purified by column chromatography
(cHex-EtOAc). (E)-3-[2-(2-Bromophenyl)-2-fluorovinyl]-2-chloropyridine as
a yellow oil, yield 0.037 g, 0.120 mmol, 57%. Rf = 0.35 (cHex-EtOAc,
5:1). IR (KBr): 3450, 3056, 2926, 1674, 1578, 1558, 1471, 1431, 1397,
1348, 1179, 1091 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 6.70 (d, JH,F = 16.7
Hz, 1 H, CH=CF), 6.92 (dd, J = 4.7, 7.7 Hz, 1 H, ArH-3'), 7.07 (ddd, J =
0.5, 1.8, 7.6 Hz, 1 H, ArH-6'), 7.27-7.30 (m, 3 H, ArH-4,5,5'), 7.62-7.66
(m, 1 H, ArH-4'), 8.19 (dd, J = 1.9, 4.7 Hz, 1 H, ArH-6). 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 107.9, 122.1, 123.4, 127.8, 128.7, 131.8, 132.0, 132.5,
133.5, 138.0, 148.2, 154.4, 160.6. 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -84.1.
MS (70 eV, EI): m/z (%) = 311/313/315 (61/80/19, [M+]), 232 (14,
[C13H8ClFN+]), 197 (100, [C13H8FN+]), 85 (27). HR-EIMS: m/z calcd for
C13H8NBrClF: 310.9512; found: 310.9510.
