$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Aldehyde 3j.30 4-Chlorobenzaldehyde (714 mg, 5.1 mmol) was
dissolved in toluene (20 mL) , and
(triphenylphosphoranylidene)acetaldehyde (1.50 g, 5 mmol) was added to
the solution. The mixture was heated at 80 °C and stirred for 24 h. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the crude product was
purified by flash column chromatography (hexane 4:1 EtOAc). 456 mg
(yield: 55%) of aldehyde 3j as a yellow solid. Spectroscopic and
analytical data are in agreement with the literature.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
